PURPOSE of /kernel/wireless_tests/functional/kernel_mdoule/kernel_module_reload/wireless_connection_to_WPA1_PEAP_AP
Description: Establish a wireless connection to a WPA1 PEAP AP, remove the kernel modules for the wireless interface, insert the kernel modules, and re-establish the connection.
Author: Ken Benoit <kbenoit@redhat.com>
Test steps:
 * Choose which wireless interface to use and describe it
 * Disable the wired network interfaces
 * Configure the test wireless interface
 * Ping the gateway address to verify connection
 * Disable the wireless interface
 * Remove the cfg80211 kernel module and dependent kernel module(s) for the wireless interface
 * Insert the cfg80211 kernel module for the wireless interface
 * Configure the test wireless interface
 * Ping the gateway address to verify connection
 * Disable the wireless interface
 * Enable the wired network interfaces
